<article>
  <h1>How we rebuilt our search</h1>
  <p>Last spring our search page was slow. People typed a word and waited. Some gave up. We knew we had to fix it, so we sat down and looked at every step between the key press and the result list.</p>
  <p>The first thing we found was simple. We sent a request on every key press. We now wait a short moment before we send it. That one change cut the load on our servers in half.</p>
</article>
